@startuml nodemedic-sequence
' NodeMedic — end-to-end flow as implemented for AFA 2026.
' Demo path on cf1z: chaos-kubelet-unhealthy → NPD detects →
' controller creates NHD → agent diagnoses → controller gates +
' cordons → Block Kit Slack → engineer clicks through to UI →
' Uncordon (or Drain via SSE) → MLC reclaims.
'
' Sequence diagrams don't need graphviz; no smetana pragma required.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888
  ParticipantBorderColor #555
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}

title NodeMedic — controller ↔ agent ↔ NHD CR ↔ on-call UI ↔ human\n(target: cf1z · Azure kubeadm; example: KubeletUnhealthy on canary node)

actor       "Operator\n(demo driver)"                          as op
participant "Worker node N\n(NPD + plugins)"                    as npd
participant "kube-apiserver\n+ NHD CRD"                         as api
participant "NodeMedic Controller\n(Spec 001 · Go)"             as ctrl
participant "NodeMedic Agent\n(Spec 002 · Python)"              as agent
participant "Agent tools\n(Bash · NR HTTP MCP · /proc · ssh ·\nkubectl · aws/az · NRQL)" as tools
participant "Slack\n(Block Kit · severity-coded)"               as slack
actor       "On-call engineer"                                  as eng
participant "On-Call UI\n(Spec 003 · Go stdlib)"                as ui
participant "MLC\n(machine-lifecycle-controller)"               as mlc

== 1. Fault injection & deterministic detection ==

op   -> npd : kubectl create job\n--from=cronjob/chaos-kubelet-unhealthy
npd  -> npd : iptables REJECT 127.0.0.1:10248\n(90s shadow window)
npd  -> npd : check-kubelet-healthz.sh\nexits 1 (every 30s tick)
npd  -> api : PATCH /nodes/N/status\nNodeCondition KubeletUnhealthy=True
npd  -> api : POST Event\n(reason=KubeletHealthzFailed)

== 2. Controller — case creation ==

api  --> ctrl : watch Node + Event\n(predicate = type ∈ watched-conditions,\n status=True transition)
ctrl -> ctrl  : debounce 30s per (node, condition)\nresolve provider/region/instanceId\n(labels + spec.providerID)\ngenerate caseId (UUIDv4)
ctrl -> api   : CREATE NodeHealthDiagnosisAI/<node>-<unix-ts>\nspec.case = {caseId, node, cluster,\n  provider, region, instanceId, trigger}\nspec.budgets = {deadline = observedAt + 5m}\nstatus.phase = "Pending"

== 3. Controller → Agent — invoke (async) ==

ctrl -> agent : POST /diagnose\n{caseId, nodeName, clusterName, trigger,\n provider, region, instanceId, budgets}\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
agent --> ctrl : 202 Accepted\n{caseId, status: "queued"}
ctrl -> api   : PATCH NHD status\nphase="Diagnosing"\ncondition[AgentInvoked]=True

== 4. Agent — diagnostic loop ==

note over agent
  Per-case ClaudeSDKClient (fresh — no cross-case state).
  permission_mode = bypassPermissions.
  Pre/PostToolUse hooks → structured stdout logs.
  No agent-side termination ceiling.
  Provider: nerd-completion gateway.
   primary  = claude-opus-4-7
   fallback = claude-sonnet-4-6
end note

loop until emit_report fires OR model halts
  agent -> tools : tool call\n(Bash kubectl/ssh/aws/az/proc OR\n NR MCP execute_nrql_query / analyze_entity_logs / ...)
  tools --> agent : raw result (4KB-truncated for evidence)
  agent -> agent : PreToolUse + PostToolUse hooks\n→ stdout JSON line per call
end

agent -> agent : emit_report (terminal tool)\n  · validate schema (confidence ∈ [0,1],\n    enum rcaCategory, enum action)\n  · build status.diagnosis payload
agent -> api   : Status().Update\nstatus.diagnosis = {rootCause,\n  rcaCategory, confidence, evidence[],\n  recommendation, modelUsed,\n  completedAt}\nstatus.phase = "Diagnosed"

== 5. Controller — confidence gate & act ==

api  --> ctrl : watch NHD update
ctrl -> ctrl  : confidenceGate(nhd):\n confidence ≥ 0.7\n ∧ |distinct evidence sources| ≥ 2\n ∧ recommendation ∈\n     {Cordon, DrainAndCordon}

alt gate passes (Applied)
  ctrl -> api  : PATCH Node N\nspec.unschedulable=true\n(cordon — idempotent)
  api  --> ctrl: ok
  ctrl -> api  : PATCH NHD status\naction.decision="Applied"\noperation="cordon"\nphase="Acted"
  ctrl -> slack: Block Kit POST\nheader=🚨 Cordoned: <node> (<cluster>)\nattachment.color=danger\nfields = {Decision, Confidence,\n         Trigger, rcaCategory}\nbutton = "View full diagnosis"\n  → <UI>/cases/<nhd-name>
else gate fails (HumanInLoop)
  ctrl -> api  : PATCH NHD status\naction.decision="HumanInLoop"\noperation="noop"\nphase="Acted"
  ctrl -> slack: Block Kit POST\nheader=⚠️ Needs review: <node> (<cluster>)\nattachment.color=warning\n(same fields + button)
end

== 5'. Late-arrival race (FR-12) — agent finishes after deadline ==

note over ctrl, agent
  If the agent did not write status.diagnosis before
  spec.budgets.deadline, the controller marks the NHD
  Failed (after retry-once is exhausted) and Slack
  posts a "Critical" message. The agent keeps running
  with no agent-side cancellation. When emit_report
  finally fires, the writer detects phase=Failed and
  REFUSES to overwrite (FR-12) — the controller's
  decision wins, and the late tool calls live in
  stdout logs (durable for the pod's lifetime only).
end note

== 6. Slack → engineer → UI (human-in-the-loop) ==

slack -> eng  : page in #cf-oncall-alerts
eng   -> ui   : click "View full diagnosis"\n(via kubectl port-forward to localhost:8080)\nGET /cases/<nhd-name>
ui    -> api  : GET NHD/<name>  + GET Node/<n>  + GET pods\n(direct apiserver reads — FR-24,\n no informer cache)
ui    --> eng : per-case page renders:\n  · case metadata\n  · rootCause (one paragraph)\n  · evidence list (collapsible)\n  · action history\n     (controller cordon + UI clicks)\n  · 3 action buttons\n     (gated by node state, not phase)

== 7. Engineer chooses next step ==

alt Uncordon (idempotent)
  eng -> ui  : click Uncordon → confirm modal
  ui  -> api : PATCH Node\nspec.unschedulable=false
  ui  -> api : PATCH NHD\nappend ui-action-history entry\n{ts, action:"uncordon",\n actor:"demo-anonymous", result:"ok"}\n(FIFO ring buffer, last-20)
  ui  --> eng: "ok — node uncordoned"\npage refreshes
  api --> mlc: watch Nodes (existing reconcile)
  mlc -> wn  : reclaim VM\n(if skipDeletion not set)
else Drain (SSE-streamed, PDB-aware)
  eng -> ui  : click Drain → confirm modal\n(modal lists pods that will be evicted)
  ui  -> api : LIST pods (filter\n  excl. DaemonSet · mirror ·\n  system-node-critical)
  loop per pod
    ui -> api  : CREATE pods/eviction
    api --> ui : 200 OR 429 (PDB violated)
    ui -> eng  : SSE event\ndata: {pod, namespace, result, detail}\n(via fetch + ReadableStream)
  end
  ui  -> eng : event: complete\ndata: {summary}
  ui  -> api : PATCH NHD\nappend ui-action-history entry\n{action:"drain",\n result:{evicted, skipped, error}}
else Clear MLC skipDeletion
  eng -> ui  : click Clear MLC skipDeletion
  ui  -> api : PATCH Node\nremove annotation\nmachine-lifecycle.newrelic.com/skipDeletion
  ui  -> api : PATCH NHD\nappend ui-action-history entry
  api --> mlc: watch Nodes
  mlc -> wn  : reclaim VM\n(next reconcile)
end

ui -> ui : structured stdout JSON log\n{event:"ui_action", ts, action,\n nhd_name, node, actor, result,\n duration_ms}

== 8. Audit / observability surface ==

eng -> api : kubectl get nhd <name> -o yaml
api --> eng: status.action (controller stamp)\n+ metadata.annotations\n  .ui-action-history (UI clicks)\n→ complete action timeline,\n  no separate audit store

note right of ui
  RBAC: 4 ClusterRole rules total —
   nodes get/list/watch/patch
   pods get/list/watch
   pods/eviction create
   nhds get/list/watch/patch
  No delete. No secrets/configmaps.
  No HTTP contract back to the
  controller; UI talks to the
  apiserver directly.
end note

note right of agent
  Hallucination guardrails (layered):
   1. emit_report schema validation
      (confidence range, enums, required
       fields, evidence non-empty).
   2. Controller confidence gate
      (Spec 001 FR-6 — ≥0.7 confidence
       AND ≥2 distinct evidence sources
       AND recommendation ∈ {Cordon, ...}).
   3. Read-only credentials
      (agent IAM/RBAC/kube-SA/NR token —
       cannot mutate cluster or cloud).
   4. Human review on the UI before
      uncordon/drain.
end note

@enduml
